<title>HONG KONG: Pacific Rim 1996 net loss HK$278.81 mln.</title>
<headline>Pacific Rim 1996 net loss HK$278.81 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 110.0 loss  vs  248.0 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  nil	   vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	3.44 gain   vs  25.87 loss</p>
<p>    Net			  278.81 loss vs  298.69 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		   431.40	vs  416.17</p>
<p>    Company name	     Pacific Rim Infrastructure Management</p>
<p>				   Enterprises Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Pacific Rim, formerly CEF Concord Holdings Ltd, is a a construction and engineering firm.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$18.1 million from unrealised net foreign exchange gain/loss on translation of the Swiss franc convertible note, loss of HK$11.87 million from realised foreign exchange loss on maturity of a foreign exchange forward contract and loss of HK$2.8 million on provision for premium on early redemption of the Swiss franc convertible note. Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
